Throughout our life the dependency doesn't disappear but rather we go on changing its capacity
up to the point of having the ability to depend horizontally, on each other; where one takes care and the other one is being cared, but also the one being cared takes care and both give.
This would be the dependency ratio ideal between adults: interdependence.
