Along with co-regulation, another variable very important is relational security.
Which is how safe I feel when I'm alone and how safe I feel when I'm with people.
Then we already know where autonomy is.
If I'm able to co-regulate myself and I'm able to be fine alone, I have autonomy capacity.
If I'm able to co-regulate myself and I'm able to be fine with others, I have privacy capacity.
And this is what we need to be able to maintain healthy adult relationships, horizontals we said, right?
People able to have autonomy and privacy.
